WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.000
- So in your book, you
talk about what happened

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:03.880
to you at the Super Bowl.

00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:04.840
Can you tell that story?

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:05.890
'Cause I mean,

00:00:05.890 --> 00:00:08.240
I have had to do that at
the Super Bowl as well

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:10.050
and it is already nerve-wracking.

00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:11.920
Can you tell everybody what happened?

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:13.610
- Yeah, what year was it?

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:17.330
It was 199- I think it was
six, I think it was 199-

00:00:17.330 --> 00:00:19.030
No, 1995.

00:00:19.030 --> 00:00:20.660
Super Bowl 29.

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:22.960
And I was asked to sing
the National Anthem

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:25.610
which is a huge honor.

00:00:25.610 --> 00:00:29.130
And yet at the same time it's terrifying.

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:31.270
There are, I mean that goes world wide

00:00:31.270 --> 00:00:32.550
and you don't even wanna,

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:34.550
Barry Manilow had said to
me right before I did it,

00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:36.750
he did it the year before and
Barry's been a great friend

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:37.583
through all these years.

00:00:37.583 --> 00:00:39.280
And he said, Kathy no matter what you do,

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:41.280
do not look up at the scoreboard

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:43.380
and look at how many people
are gonna be watching.

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:44.213
Don't do it.

00:00:44.213 --> 00:00:46.378
- Oh good Lord, don't tell her that.

00:00:46.378 --> 00:00:47.211
(laughs)

00:00:47.211 --> 00:00:48.920
- Yeah, well I'll tell you the story.

00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:52.170
It was, we have something called
Final Looks in our business

00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:55.500
which is, we're ready to go,
hair makeup get over there,

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:57.700
do whatever final touches you're gonna do

00:00:57.700 --> 00:00:59.300
'cause it's go, we're ready.

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:04.300
And so my hairdresser, by mistake,

00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:05.570
does hair spray on me

00:01:05.570 --> 00:01:07.430
and goes in my right eye.

00:01:07.430 --> 00:01:10.090
Boom, right in my right eye and
I'm going blinded from that.

00:01:10.090 --> 00:01:12.970
And then my makeup artist is working on me

00:01:12.970 --> 00:01:14.943
one the other side and she has a-

00:01:16.474 --> 00:01:17.307
- [Kelly] A wand.

00:01:17.307 --> 00:01:20.340
- A mascara wand, boom,
right into my left eye.

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:24.283
So I'm walking out like,
they had to lead me.

00:01:26.350 --> 00:01:29.161
They don't wait for you at the Super Bowl.

00:01:29.161 --> 00:01:32.850
So they're leading me out and
I can hear everybody scream

00:01:32.850 --> 00:01:34.360
and I can hear all this noise

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:37.410
and I'm going, oh Jesus,
help me Jesus, help me.

00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:41.320
I get there and then of course
the orchestration starts.

00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:43.580
You can hear the
orchestra, full orchestra.

00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:45.270
And it's time for me to sing,

00:01:45.270 --> 00:01:50.270
of all the lyrics, "Oh say can you" what?

00:01:50.441 --> 00:01:51.310
See.
(audience laughs)

00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:53.921
And I'm going, no, I can't see,

00:01:53.921 --> 00:01:55.450
(laughs)

00:01:55.450 --> 00:01:57.250
- [Kelly] Oh my God, that's awesome.

